From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:11:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/rockchip: Leave an attach-only IOMMU alone on runtime
 PM

The RK3528 VOP's IOMMU answers register reads only once the VOP has set
itself up, yet the driver core resumes it, as the VOP's supplier, before
the VOP's probe: the first read never completes and locks up the CPU.
With rockchip,disable-device-link-resume, runtime resume and suspend
leave the IOMMU alone, and the master's attach and detach, which run
with the master set up, enable and disable it.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
index 21af2f6..228208b 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
@@ -112,6 +112,7 @@ struct rk_iommu {
 	struct clk_bulk_data *clocks;
 	int num_clocks;
 	bool reset_disabled;
+	bool attach_only; /* enabled and disabled by its master's attach alone */
 	struct iommu_device iommu;
 	struct list_head node; /* entry in rk_iommu_domain.iommus */
 	struct iommu_domain *domain; /* domain to which iommu is attached */
@@ -1259,6 +1260,8 @@ static int rk_iommu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	iommu->reset_disabled = device_property_read_bool(dev,
 					"rockchip,disable-mmu-reset");
+	iommu->attach_only = device_property_read_bool(dev,
+					"rockchip,disable-device-link-resume");
 
 	/*
 	 * Take every clock the devicetree provides.  Most IOMMU instances
@@ -1332,7 +1335,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused rk_iommu_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct rk_iommu *iommu = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	if (iommu->domain == &rk_identity_domain)
+	if (iommu->domain == &rk_identity_domain || iommu->attach_only)
 		return 0;
 
 	rk_iommu_disable(iommu);
@@ -1343,7 +1346,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused rk_iommu_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct rk_iommu *iommu = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	if (iommu->domain == &rk_identity_domain)
+	if (iommu->domain == &rk_identity_domain || iommu->attach_only)
 		return 0;
 
 	return rk_iommu_enable(iommu);
